{"t": 1792426593.1637805, "event": "data_level", "data": {"name": "Shadow Kin", "oracle_text": "Flash\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, each player mills three cards. You may exile a creature card from among the cards milled this way. If you do, this creature becomes a copy of that card, except it has this ability.", "mana_cost": {"type": "Cost", "shards": ["Blue"], "generic": 3}, "chain": [{"trigger": "Phase", "phase": "Upkeep", "effect": "Mill", "mill_count": 3, "mill_target": "Controller", "player_scope": "All"}, {"sub": "ChangeZone", "origin": null, "destination": "Exile", "target": {"type": "Typed", "type_filters": ["Creature"], "controller": null, "properties": []}, "optional": true}, {"sub2": "BecomeCopy", "target": "ParentTarget", "mods": [{"type": "RetainPrintedTriggerFromSource", "source_trigger_index": 0}], "condition": {"type": "EffectOutcome", "signal": "OptionalEffectPerformed"}}], "parse_ok": true, "data_notes": ["Mill target is Controller (not EachPlayer) with player_scope=All; on v0.81.3 the each-player mill worked behaviorally (each library -3).", "ChangeZone origin=null: no graveyard zone or event-set provenance in the parse -- the triage's data-level finding persists on v0.113.0; the behavioral question is whether the engine scopes candidates to the milled set anyway."]}}
